===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To make a clashing sound.
#: {{ux|en|The cymbals '''clashed'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cause to make a clashing sound.
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To come into violent [[conflict]].
#: {{syn|en|collide}}
#: {{ux|en|Fans from opposing teams '''clashed''' on the streets after the game.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[argue]] angrily.
#: {{ux|en|My parents often '''clashed''' about minor things, such as the cleaning or shopping [[rota]].}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|in games or sports}} To [[face]] each other in an important game.
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=June 27, 2008
|author=
|title=Jones confirms Calzaghe showdown
|work=BBC Sport
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/boxing/7476878.stm
|page=
|passage=The veteran American legend claims he and Welsh two-weight world champion Calzaghe will '''clash''' on 20 September, probably at The MGM Grand in Las Vegas.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251017224255/http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/boxing/7476878.stm|archivedate=17 October 2025}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|of clothes, decor, colours}} To fail to look good together; to contrast unattractively; to fail to harmonize.
#: {{ux|en|You can't wear that shirt! It '''clashes''' with your trousers.}}
#: {{ux|en|The hotel room was ugly, and the wallpaper '''clashed''' with the carpet.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|of events}} To [[coincide]], to happen at the same time, thereby rendering it impossible to attend all.
#: {{ux|en|I can't come to your wedding because it '''clashes''' with a friend's funeral.}}
#: {{ux|en|I wanted to take German, but it '''clashed''' with art on the timetable.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|Scotland}} To [[chatter]] or [[gossip]].
# {{lb|en|intransitive|slang|video games}} To play ''{{w|Clash Royale}}'' or ''{{w|Clash of Clans}}''.
#: {{ux|en|Dude, are we '''clashing''' tonight?}}
#: {{ux|en|Let's '''clash''' before bedtime.}}

