==English==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|en|enm|deliberat|alt=deliberat(e)}}, {{bor+|enm|la|dēlīberātus|nocap=1|nocat=1}}, {{glossary|perfect}} {{glossary|passive}} {{glossary|participle}} of {{m|la|dēlīberō||to consider, weigh well}} (see {{af|en|-ate|id1=adjective|pos1=adjective-forming suffix}} and {{af|en|-ate|id1=verb|pos1=verb-forming suffix}}), from  {{affix|la|dē-|*līberō|nocat=1}} / {{m|la|lībrō||to weigh}}), from {{m|la|*libera}} / {{m|la|libra||a balance}}; see {{m|en|librate}}. {{dbt|en|deliber}}.

===Pronunciation 1===
* {{enPR|dĭlĭbʹ(ə)rət}}, {{IPA|en|/dɪˈlɪb.(ə.)ɹət/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/dɪˈlɪb.ɚ.ət/|/dɪˈlɪb.(ə.)ɹət/|a=GA,CA}}
** {{enPR|dəlĭbʹ(ə)rət|a=weak vowel}}, {{IPA|en|/dəˈlɪb.ɚ.ət/|/dəˈlɪb.(ə.)ɹət/}}
* {{IPA|en|/dɪˈlɪb.ə.ɹət/|[dɪˈlɪb.ɹət]|a=California}}
** {{IPA|en|[dɪˈlɪb.ɹɪt]|[dɪˈlɪb.ɹɛt]|a=weak vowel|q2=California Vowel Shift}}
*** {{audio|en|en-us-deliberate-adj.ogg|IPA=[dɪˈlɪb.ɹɛt]}}
* {{IPA|en|/dəˈlɪb.(ə.)ɹət/|a=AU}}
* {{IPA|en|/dəˈləb.(ə.)ɹət/|a=NZ}}
* {{hyph|en|de|lib|er|ate}}

====Adjective====
{{en-adj}}

# Done on [[purpose]]; [[intentional]].
#: {{syn|en|purposeful|volitional|Thesaurus:intentional}}
#: {{ant|en|unintentional|unwitting}}
#: {{ux|en|a '''deliberate''' attempt to cover up his crime}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|text=The massacre of up to 8,000 Bosnian Muslims at Srebrenica in 1995 was an act of genocide in a '''deliberate''' attempt by the Bosnian Serb leadership to exterminate part of the Muslim community, appeal judges ruled in a crucial case at the international war crimes tribunal in The Hague yesterday.|title=Hague rules Srebrenica was act of genocide|url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2004/apr/20/warcrimes|date=2004-04-20|author=Ian Traynor|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261024111700/https://www.theguardian.com/world/2004/apr/20/warcrimes|archivedate=24 October 2026}}
# Formed with [[deliberation]]; carefully considered; not [[sudden]] or [[rash]].
#: {{syn|en|careful|cautious|well-advised|Thesaurus:cautious}}
#: {{ux|en|a '''deliberate''' opinion; a '''deliberate''' measure or result}}
# Of a person, weighing [[facts]] and [[arguments]] with a view to a choice or decision; carefully considering the probable [[consequence]]s of a step; slow in determining.
#: {{syn|en|circumspect|thoughtful}}
#: {{ux|en|The jury took eight hours to come to its '''deliberate''' verdict.}}
# Not [[hasty]] or [[sudden]]; slow.

